exports[`report > renders markdown and html 1`] = `
"# Journey coverage report

13 journeys · 7 full · 5 partial · 1 manual · from \`all-journeys-alpha.json\`

| Journey | Steps | Coverage | Main note |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Agent | 0 | Full | Headers only (Zero Page Login) |
| DemoPreferencesSub | 1 | Full |  |
| DemoSignup | 6 | Full | Random Challenge Picker: 3 variants, solved at run time |
| DemoVerifySub | 1 | Full | Random Challenge Picker: 3 variants, solved at run time |
| ForgottenUsername | 2 (+1 optional) | Partial | Stops at Email Suspend Node |
| frAuth2 | 3 | Partial | Step 3 needs IN_TOTP_SECRET or IN_OTP (one-time code) |
| Login | 1 (+1 optional) | Full | ProgressiveProfile step is optional |
| passwordless2 | 2 | Manual | WebAuthn Authentication Node: needs a person |
| ProgressiveProfile | 0 (+1 optional) | Full | ProgressiveProfile step is optional |
| Registration | 1 | Partial | Stops at Email Suspend Node |
| ResetPassword | 2 | Partial | Stops at Email Suspend Node |
| test-journeys-001 | 2 | Full |  |
| UpdatePassword | 2 | Partial | Needs a session: \`--with-session Login\` |

## Notes and warnings

### ForgottenUsername

- Stops at step 2 (Email Suspend Node) until the email link is opened

### frAuth2

- Step 3 needs IN_TOTP_SECRET or IN_OTP (one-time code)

### passwordless2

- Step 2 (WebAuthn Authentication Node) needs a person: Needs a security key or passkey in a browser; cannot be completed with curl

### Registration

- Stops at step 2 (Email Suspend Node) until the email link is opened
- **info** KBA Definition: KBA question count is not in the export; assuming 1 (set "kbaCount" in bk.config.json)

### ResetPassword

- Stops at step 2 (Email Suspend Node) until the email link is opened

### UpdatePassword

- Step 1 may stop for an email link (variant false)
- Needs an existing session: generate with --with-session Login
"
`;

exports[`runbook > Agent.runbook.md 1`] = `
"# Agent – runbook

Generated by bkj2c from \`all-journeys-alpha.json\`. Target: **Success** · Coverage: **FULL** · Steps: **0**

## Setup

\`\`\`bash
export TENANT=https://tenant.example.com
rm -f cookies.txt   # one cookie jar per run keeps the session and load-balancer affinity
\`\`\`

Each call posts back the whole previous response (\`authId\` plus \`callbacks\`) with the \`input\` values filled in.

| Variable | Default | Used for |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`IN_USERNAME\` | \`CHANGE_ME\` | Sent as a request header (Zero Page Login) |
| \`IN_PASSWORD\` | _(secret)_ | Sent as a request header (Zero Page Login) |

## Start

\`\`\`bash
curl -X POST "$TENANT/am/json/realms/root/realms/alpha/authenticate?authIndexType=service&authIndexValue=Agent" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Accept-API-Version: resource=2.0, protocol=1.0" \\
  -H "X-OpenAM-Username: <IN_USERNAME>" \\
  -H "X-OpenAM-Password: <IN_PASSWORD>" \\
  -b cookies.txt -c cookies.txt \\
  -d '{}'
\`\`\`

**Expected next:** \`tokenId\` (journey finished: Success)
"
`;

exports[`runbook > DemoSignup.runbook.md 1`] = `
"# DemoSignup – runbook

Generated by bkj2c from \`all-journeys-alpha.json\`. Target: **Success** · Coverage: **FULL** · Steps: **6**

## Setup

\`\`\`bash
export TENANT=https://tenant.example.com
rm -f cookies.txt   # one cookie jar per run keeps the session and load-balancer affinity
\`\`\`

Each call posts back the whole previous response (\`authId\` plus \`callbacks\`) with the \`input\` values filled in.

| Variable | Default | Used for |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`IN_CHANNEL\` | \`0\` | ChoiceCallback "Which channel are you signing up from?" — step 1, DemoSignup / Choose Channel |
| \`IN_USERNAME\` | \`CHANGE_ME\` | ValidatedCreateUsernameCallback "Username" — step 2, DemoSignup / Registration Page |
| \`IN_GIVENNAME\` | \`CHANGE_ME\` | StringAttributeInputCallback "givenName" — step 2, DemoSignup / Registration Page |
| \`IN_SN\` | \`CHANGE_ME\` | StringAttributeInputCallback "sn" — step 2, DemoSignup / Registration Page |
| \`IN_MAIL\` | \`change.me@example.com\` | StringAttributeInputCallback "mail" — step 2, DemoSignup / Registration Page |
| \`IN_PASSWORD\` | _(secret)_ | ValidatedCreatePasswordCallback "Password" — step 2, DemoSignup / Registration Page |
| \`IN_TERMS_CONSENT\` | \`0\` | ConfirmationCallback — step 4, DemoSignup / Terms Consent |
| \`IN_CITY\` | \`CHANGE_ME\` | NameCallback "City" — step 5, DemoPreferencesSub / Collect Preferences |
| \`IN_PREFERRED_LANGUAGE\` | \`0\` | ChoiceCallback "Preferred language" — step 5, DemoPreferencesSub / Collect Preferences |

## Start

\`\`\`bash
curl -X POST "$TENANT/am/json/realms/root/realms/alpha/authenticate?authIndexType=service&authIndexValue=DemoSignup" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Accept-API-Version: resource=2.0, protocol=1.0" \\
  -b cookies.txt -c cookies.txt \\
  -d '{}'
\`\`\`

**Expected next:** \`TextOutputCallback,ChoiceCallback\`

## Step 1 – Choose Channel (submit)

> Which channel are you signing up from (web, mobile, partner)

| Input | Callback | Value |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`IDToken2\` | ChoiceCallback "Which channel are you signing up from?" | \`IN_CHANNEL\` |

\`\`\`bash
curl -X POST "$TENANT/am/json/realms/root/realms/alpha/authenticate?authIndexType=service&authIndexValue=DemoSignup" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Accept-API-Version: resource=2.0, protocol=1.0" \\
  -b cookies.txt -c cookies.txt \\
  -d '{"authId":"<authId from the start call>","callbacks":[
    {"type":"TextOutputCallback","output":[{"name":"message","value":"Welcome to the demo signup journey."},{"name":"messageType","value":"0"}],"input":[]},
    {"type":"ChoiceCallback","output":[{"name":"prompt","value":"Which channel are you signing up from?"},{"name":"choices","value":["web","mobile","partner"]},{"name":"defaultChoice","value":0}],"input":[{"name":"IDToken2","value":0}]}]}'
\`\`\`

**Expected next:** \`ValidatedCreateUsernameCallback,StringAttributeInputCallback,StringAttributeInputCallback,StringAttributeInputCallback,ValidatedCreatePasswordCallback\`

## Step 2 – Registration Page (submit)

> Choose a username, enter your first name, enter your last name, enter your email address and choose a password

| Input | Callback | Value |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`IDToken1\` | ValidatedCreateUsernameCallback "Username" | \`IN_USERNAME\` |
| \`IDToken2\` | StringAttributeInputCallback "givenName" | \`IN_GIVENNAME\` |
| \`IDToken3\` | StringAttributeInputCallback "sn" | \`IN_SN\` |
| \`IDToken4\` | StringAttributeInputCallback "mail" | \`IN_MAIL\` |
| \`IDToken5\` | ValidatedCreatePasswordCallback "Password" | \`IN_PASSWORD\` |

\`\`\`bash
curl -X POST "$TENANT/am/json/realms/root/realms/alpha/authenticate?authIndexType=service&authIndexValue=DemoSignup" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Accept-API-Version: resource=2.0, protocol=1.0" \\
  -b cookies.txt -c cookies.txt \\
  -d '{"authId":"<authId from step 1>","callbacks":[
    {"type":"ValidatedCreateUsernameCallback","output":[{"name":"prompt","value":"Username"}],"input":[{"name":"IDToken1","value":"<IN_USERNAME>"},{"name":"IDToken1validateOnly","value":false}]},
    {"type":"StringAttributeInputCallback","output":[{"name":"name","value":"givenName"},{"name":"prompt","value":"givenName"},{"name":"required","value":true}],"input":[{"name":"IDToken2","value":"<IN_GIVENNAME>"},{"name":"IDToken2validateOnly","value":false}]},
    {"type":"StringAttributeInputCallback","output":[{"name":"name","value":"sn"},{"name":"prompt","value":"sn"},{"name":"required","value":true}],"input":[{"name":"IDToken3","value":"<IN_SN>"},{"name":"IDToken3validateOnly","value":false}]},
    {"type":"StringAttributeInputCallback","output":[{"name":"name","value":"mail"},{"name":"prompt","value":"mail"},{"name":"required","value":true}],"input":[{"name":"IDToken4","value":"<IN_MAIL>"},{"name":"IDToken4validateOnly","value":false}]},
    {"type":"ValidatedCreatePasswordCallback","output":[{"name":"prompt","value":"Password"}],"input":[{"name":"IDToken5","value":"<IN_PASSWORD>"},{"name":"IDToken5validateOnly","value":false}]}]}'
\`\`\`

**Expected next:** \`NameCallback\` (math) or \`TextOutputCallback,NameCallback\` (phrase) or \`HiddenValueCallback,PasswordCallback\` (pin)

## Step 3 – DemoVerifySub / Random Challenge Picker (variant)

> The system gives you one of 3 quick challenges (math, phrase, pin) and checks your answer

Random Challenge Picker decides on the server (random), so it sends one of these. Match the callback types you received:

### Variant \`math\` – \`NameCallback\` – adds the two numbers in the prompt

| Input | Callback | Value |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`IDToken1\` | NameCallback "Math challenge: what is {a} + {b}?" | adds the two numbers in the prompt |

\`\`\`bash
curl -X POST "$TENANT/am/json/realms/root/realms/alpha/authenticate?authIndexType=service&authIndexValue=DemoSignup" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Accept-API-Version: resource=2.0, protocol=1.0" \\
  -b cookies.txt -c cookies.txt \\
  -d '{"authId":"<authId from step 2>","callbacks":[
    {"type":"NameCallback","output":[{"name":"prompt","value":"Math challenge: what is {a} + {b}?"}],"input":[{"name":"IDToken1","value":"<computed: math-sum>"}]}]}'
\`\`\`

### Variant \`phrase\` – \`TextOutputCallback,NameCallback\` – copies the last word of the message

| Input | Callback | Value |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`IDToken2\` | NameCallback "Type the word shown above" | copies the last word of the message |

\`\`\`bash
curl -X POST "$TENANT/am/json/realms/root/realms/alpha/authenticate?authIndexType=service&authIndexValue=DemoSignup" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Accept-API-Version: resource=2.0, protocol=1.0" \\
  -b cookies.txt -c cookies.txt \\
  -d '{"authId":"<authId from step 2>","callbacks":[
    {"type":"TextOutputCallback","output":[{"name":"message","value":"Phrase challenge: your word is {w}"},{"name":"messageType","value":"0"}],"input":[]},
    {"type":"NameCallback","output":[{"name":"prompt","value":"Type the word shown above"}],"input":[{"name":"IDToken2","value":"<computed: echo-text>"}]}]}'
\`\`\`

### Variant \`pin\` – \`HiddenValueCallback,PasswordCallback\` – sends back the hidden value

| Input | Callback | Value |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`IDToken1\` | HiddenValueCallback "demoPin" | sent back unchanged |
| \`IDToken2\` | PasswordCallback "PIN challenge: send back the value of the hidden demoPin field" | sends back the hidden value |

\`\`\`bash
curl -X POST "$TENANT/am/json/realms/root/realms/alpha/authenticate?authIndexType=service&authIndexValue=DemoSignup" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Accept-API-Version: resource=2.0, protocol=1.0" \\
  -b cookies.txt -c cookies.txt \\
  -d '{"authId":"<authId from step 2>","callbacks":[
    {"type":"HiddenValueCallback","output":[{"name":"value","value":"<value from the server>"},{"name":"id","value":"demoPin"}],"input":[{"name":"IDToken1","value":"<value from the server>"}]},
    {"type":"PasswordCallback","output":[{"name":"prompt","value":"PIN challenge: send back the value of the hidden demoPin field"}],"input":[{"name":"IDToken2","value":"<computed: echo-hidden>"}]}]}'
\`\`\`

**Expected next:** \`TextOutputCallback,ConfirmationCallback\`

## Step 4 – Terms Consent (submit)

> Choose Accept or Decline

| Input | Callback | Value |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`IDToken2\` | ConfirmationCallback | \`IN_TERMS_CONSENT\` |

\`\`\`bash
curl -X POST "$TENANT/am/json/realms/root/realms/alpha/authenticate?authIndexType=service&authIndexValue=DemoSignup" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Accept-API-Version: resource=2.0, protocol=1.0" \\
  -b cookies.txt -c cookies.txt \\
  -d '{"authId":"<authId from step 3>","callbacks":[
    {"type":"TextOutputCallback","output":[{"name":"message","value":"Do you accept the demo terms?"},{"name":"messageType","value":"0"}],"input":[]},
    {"type":"ConfirmationCallback","output":[{"name":"prompt","value":""},{"name":"messageType","value":0},{"name":"options","value":["Accept","Decline"]},{"name":"optionType","value":-1},{"name":"defaultOption","value":0}],"input":[{"name":"IDToken2","value":0}]}]}'
\`\`\`

**Expected next:** \`NameCallback,ChoiceCallback\`

## Step 5 – DemoPreferencesSub / Collect Preferences (submit)

> Enter city and preferred language (en, th, ja)

| Input | Callback | Value |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`IDToken1\` | NameCallback "City" | \`IN_CITY\` |
| \`IDToken2\` | ChoiceCallback "Preferred language" | \`IN_PREFERRED_LANGUAGE\` |

\`\`\`bash
curl -X POST "$TENANT/am/json/realms/root/realms/alpha/authenticate?authIndexType=service&authIndexValue=DemoSignup" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Accept-API-Version: resource=2.0, protocol=1.0" \\
  -b cookies.txt -c cookies.txt \\
  -d '{"authId":"<authId from step 4>","callbacks":[
    {"type":"NameCallback","output":[{"name":"prompt","value":"City"}],"input":[{"name":"IDToken1","value":"<IN_CITY>"}]},
    {"type":"ChoiceCallback","output":[{"name":"prompt","value":"Preferred language"},{"name":"choices","value":["en","th","ja"]},{"name":"defaultChoice","value":0}],"input":[{"name":"IDToken2","value":0}]}]}'
\`\`\`

**Expected next:** \`TextOutputCallback\`

## Step 6 – Show Summary (submit)

> Read the message ("Account ready. Channel: …, challenge: …") and continue

_No inputs: post the response back as received._

\`\`\`bash
curl -X POST "$TENANT/am/json/realms/root/realms/alpha/authenticate?authIndexType=service&authIndexValue=DemoSignup" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Accept-API-Version: resource=2.0, protocol=1.0" \\
  -b cookies.txt -c cookies.txt \\
  -d '{"authId":"<authId from step 5>","callbacks":[
    {"type":"TextOutputCallback","output":[{"name":"message","value":"Account ready. Channel: {nodeState.get(demoChannel)}, challenge: {nodeState.get(demoChallenge)}"},{"name":"messageType","value":"0"}],"input":[]}]}'
\`\`\`

**Expected next:** \`tokenId\` (journey finished: Success)
"
`;

exports[`runbook > Login.runbook.md 1`] = `
"# Login – runbook

Generated by bkj2c from \`all-journeys-alpha.json\`. Target: **Success** · Coverage: **FULL** · Steps: **2**

## Setup

\`\`\`bash
export TENANT=https://tenant.example.com
rm -f cookies.txt   # one cookie jar per run keeps the session and load-balancer affinity
\`\`\`

Each call posts back the whole previous response (\`authId\` plus \`callbacks\`) with the \`input\` values filled in.

| Variable | Default | Used for |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`IN_USERNAME\` | \`CHANGE_ME\` | NameCallback "User Name" — step 1, Login / Page Node (Sign In) |
| \`IN_PASSWORD\` | _(secret)_ | PasswordCallback "Password" — step 1, Login / Page Node (Sign In) |
| \`IN_PREF_UPDATES\` | \`false\` | BooleanAttributeInputCallback "preferences/updates" — step 2, ProgressiveProfile / Page Node (Please select your preferences) |
| \`IN_PREF_MARKETING\` | \`false\` | BooleanAttributeInputCallback "preferences/marketing" — step 2, ProgressiveProfile / Page Node (Please select your preferences) |

## Start

\`\`\`bash
curl -X POST "$TENANT/am/json/realms/root/realms/alpha/authenticate?authIndexType=service&authIndexValue=Login" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Accept-API-Version: resource=2.0, protocol=1.0" \\
  -b cookies.txt -c cookies.txt \\
  -d '{}'
\`\`\`

**Expected next:** \`NameCallback,PasswordCallback\`

## Step 1 – Page Node (Sign In) (submit)

> Sign in with your username and password

| Input | Callback | Value |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`IDToken1\` | NameCallback "User Name" | \`IN_USERNAME\` |
| \`IDToken2\` | PasswordCallback "Password" | \`IN_PASSWORD\` |

\`\`\`bash
curl -X POST "$TENANT/am/json/realms/root/realms/alpha/authenticate?authIndexType=service&authIndexValue=Login" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Accept-API-Version: resource=2.0, protocol=1.0" \\
  -b cookies.txt -c cookies.txt \\
  -d '{"authId":"<authId from the start call>","callbacks":[
    {"type":"NameCallback","output":[{"name":"prompt","value":"User Name"}],"input":[{"name":"IDToken1","value":"<IN_USERNAME>"}]},
    {"type":"PasswordCallback","output":[{"name":"prompt","value":"Password"}],"input":[{"name":"IDToken2","value":"<IN_PASSWORD>"}]}]}'
\`\`\`

**Expected next:** \`BooleanAttributeInputCallback,BooleanAttributeInputCallback\` (optional step 2) or \`tokenId\` (journey finished: Success)

## Step 2 – ProgressiveProfile / Page Node (Please select your preferences) (optional)

> If asked: choose whether to receive updates and choose whether to receive marketing emails (only when it is login number 3, and the user matches "!(/preferences pr) or /preferences/marketing eq false or /preferences/updates eq false")

**Optional:** appears only when it is login number 3, and the user matches "!(/preferences pr) or /preferences/marketing eq false or /preferences/updates eq false". If the response has other callbacks, skip this step.

| Input | Callback | Value |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`IDToken1\` | BooleanAttributeInputCallback "preferences/updates" | \`IN_PREF_UPDATES\` |
| \`IDToken2\` | BooleanAttributeInputCallback "preferences/marketing" | \`IN_PREF_MARKETING\` |

\`\`\`bash
curl -X POST "$TENANT/am/json/realms/root/realms/alpha/authenticate?authIndexType=service&authIndexValue=Login" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Accept-API-Version: resource=2.0, protocol=1.0" \\
  -b cookies.txt -c cookies.txt \\
  -d '{"authId":"<authId from step 1>","callbacks":[
    {"type":"BooleanAttributeInputCallback","output":[{"name":"name","value":"preferences/updates"},{"name":"prompt","value":"preferences/updates"},{"name":"required","value":true}],"input":[{"name":"IDToken1","value":false},{"name":"IDToken1validateOnly","value":false}]},
    {"type":"BooleanAttributeInputCallback","output":[{"name":"name","value":"preferences/marketing"},{"name":"prompt","value":"preferences/marketing"},{"name":"required","value":true}],"input":[{"name":"IDToken2","value":false},{"name":"IDToken2validateOnly","value":false}]}]}'
\`\`\`

**Expected next:** \`tokenId\` (journey finished: Success)
"
`;

exports[`runbook > UpdatePassword.runbook.md 1`] = `
"# UpdatePassword – runbook

Generated by bkj2c from \`all-journeys-alpha.json\`. Target: **Success** · Coverage: **PARTIAL** · Steps: **2**

- Step 1 may stop for an email link (variant false)
- Needs an existing session: generate with --with-session Login

## Setup

\`\`\`bash
export TENANT=https://tenant.example.com
rm -f cookies.txt   # one cookie jar per run keeps the session and load-balancer affinity
\`\`\`

Each call posts back the whole previous response (\`authId\` plus \`callbacks\`) with the \`input\` values filled in.

| Variable | Default | Used for |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`IN_PASSWORD\` | _(secret)_ | PasswordCallback "Password" — step 1, UpdatePassword / Attribute Present Decision (variant true) |
| \`IN_NEW_PASSWORD\` | _(secret)_ | ValidatedCreatePasswordCallback "Password" — step 2, UpdatePassword / Page Node (Update Password) |

**Session:** this journey needs an existing session. Run a login journey first with the same \`cookies.txt\`.

## Start

\`\`\`bash
curl -X POST "$TENANT/am/json/realms/root/realms/alpha/authenticate?authIndexType=service&authIndexValue=UpdatePassword" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Accept-API-Version: resource=2.0, protocol=1.0" \\
  -b cookies.txt -c cookies.txt \\
  -d '{}'
\`\`\`

**Expected next:** \`PasswordCallback\` (true) or \`SuspendedTextOutputCallback\` (false)

## Step 1 – Attribute Present Decision (variant)

> Depending on your account, enter your password, or check your email and click the link

Attribute Present Decision decides on the server (user data), so it sends one of these. Match the callback types you received:

### Variant \`true\` – \`PasswordCallback\`

| Input | Callback | Value |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`IDToken1\` | PasswordCallback "Password" | \`IN_PASSWORD\` |

\`\`\`bash
curl -X POST "$TENANT/am/json/realms/root/realms/alpha/authenticate?authIndexType=service&authIndexValue=UpdatePassword" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Accept-API-Version: resource=2.0, protocol=1.0" \\
  -b cookies.txt -c cookies.txt \\
  -d '{"authId":"<authId from the start call>","callbacks":[
    {"type":"PasswordCallback","output":[{"name":"prompt","value":"Password"}],"input":[{"name":"IDToken1","value":"<IN_PASSWORD>"}]}]}'
\`\`\`

### Variant \`false\` – \`SuspendedTextOutputCallback\`

The journey is suspended and an email was sent. Open the link from the email, or take its \`suspendedId\` and continue with:

\`\`\`bash
curl -X POST "$TENANT/am/json/realms/root/realms/alpha/authenticate?authIndexType=service&authIndexValue=UpdatePassword&suspendedId=<suspendedId>" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Accept-API-Version: resource=2.0, protocol=1.0" \\
  -b cookies.txt -c cookies.txt \\
  -d '{}'
\`\`\`

**Expected next:** \`ValidatedCreatePasswordCallback\`

## Step 2 – Page Node (Update Password) (submit)

> Choose a password

| Input | Callback | Value |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`IDToken1\` | ValidatedCreatePasswordCallback "Password" | \`IN_NEW_PASSWORD\` |

\`\`\`bash
curl -X POST "$TENANT/am/json/realms/root/realms/alpha/authenticate?authIndexType=service&authIndexValue=UpdatePassword" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Accept-API-Version: resource=2.0, protocol=1.0" \\
  -b cookies.txt -c cookies.txt \\
  -d '{"authId":"<authId from step 1>","callbacks":[
    {"type":"ValidatedCreatePasswordCallback","output":[{"name":"prompt","value":"Password"}],"input":[{"name":"IDToken1","value":"<IN_NEW_PASSWORD>"},{"name":"IDToken1validateOnly","value":false}]}]}'
\`\`\`

**Expected next:** \`tokenId\` (journey finished: Success)
"
`;
